kunzite: Adreno 710 step 19, the GPU's SMMU context, ring and SQE microcode (kgpu=19; the port map's 18).
19 continues kgsl's gen7_gpu_boot with GX on from step 18 (OOB_GPU held): H2F_MSG_START (10, the
header alone) as gen7_gmu_hfi_start_msg sends it after the OOB set, acked with result 0. Then
kgsl_mmu_start's part, done as step 13 did for the GMU: stream 0 (FDT gfx3d_user, mask 0x400) ->
HLOS SMR/S2CR entry 0 -> context 0 (the GPU's in kgsl and Linux), on the same 3-level tables as
the GMU with ASID 0; the GPU's addresses start at 4 GiB (root entry 4, away from the GMU's), so the
table pool grows from 8 to 12. In GPU memory: the ringbuffer (KGSL_RB_SIZE 32K at 0x100000000,
filled with 0xaa as gen7_rb_start does), a scratch page (0x100008000) and adreno_get_firmware's
copy of /usr/share/firmware/kunzite/a710_sqe.fw (all but its first word, at 0x100010000; the
version word printed as get_ucode_version reads it). Context 0 is programmed and kept like
context 1 (SCTLR 0 first, CBA2R/CBAR/TCR2/TCR/TTBR0/TTBR1/MAIR), its FSR cleared, TLBIASID on
contexts 0 and 1 (new tables under the shared root), sync; then on, S2CR0 and SMR0, all read back.
Last, gen7_rb_start's CP_RB_BASE/_HI and CP_SQE_INSTR_BASE_LO/_HI (GX registers; they go with GX
in the slumber), read back; CP_SQE_CNTL is left alone, the CP stays halted (its start is the port
map's 20). Undo (before step 18's OOB clear and slumber): SMR0 and S2CR0 back, CB0 off, the
memory freed. Also: the teardown no longer zeroes kg.step, so lines from the undo (the slumber's
HFI message) carry the last step's number instead of 0.

